WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:03.002
-My next guest
is a very funny comedian

00:00:03.002 --> 00:00:05.405
and "New York Times"
best-selling author.

00:00:05.405 --> 00:00:08.607
She has a new show called "Doing
the Most with Phoebe Robinson,"

00:00:08.607 --> 00:00:12.211
which airs Fridays at 11:00 p.m.
on Comedy Central.

00:00:12.211 --> 00:00:14.813
Please welcome Phoebe Robinson!

00:00:14.813 --> 00:00:17.717
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah!

00:00:17.717 --> 00:00:19.118
Come on now.

00:00:19.118 --> 00:00:21.121
Welcome. Welcome.

00:00:21.121 --> 00:00:23.189
Thank you for coming back
to our show, pal.

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:25.758
I appreciate it.
-Thanks for having me.

00:00:25.758 --> 00:00:29.963
-Phoebe, this is your third time
on our show since the pandemic.

00:00:29.963 --> 00:00:31.664
We've seen each other
through different stages

00:00:31.664 --> 00:00:32.832
of the quarantine.

00:00:32.832 --> 00:00:35.234
How are you right now?
How are you feeling?

00:00:35.234 --> 00:00:38.204
-I'm over it, Jimmy.
I want to get out, okay?

00:00:38.204 --> 00:00:39.972
-I know. Okay. Yes.

00:00:39.972 --> 00:00:42.108
-I want to go to a concert.
-Okay.

00:00:42.108 --> 00:00:45.210
-Smell some B.O.
I don't care who's playing.

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:46.913
Okay, it can Chumbawamba.

00:00:46.913 --> 00:00:49.482
I want to be out
in these streets.

00:00:49.482 --> 00:00:50.750
I'm done.
-You're done.

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:52.485
Okay, I got you.
Okay, I hear you.

00:00:52.485 --> 00:00:55.254
I saw you posted this photo
that made me laugh.

00:00:55.254 --> 00:00:58.224
You said, "I just want everyone
to know that this is what

00:00:58.224 --> 00:01:00.159
I'm wearing when it's time
to get my vaccine."

00:01:00.159 --> 00:01:02.429
-Yeah. Mm-hmm.
-That's what I'm talking about.

00:01:02.429 --> 00:01:04.664
Ooh, la, la!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:04.664 --> 00:01:08.601
-Look at those tiny boobies
just out and proud.

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:10.069
[ Laughter ]
Love it.

00:01:10.069 --> 00:01:13.306
-Phoebe, I heard that you got
your first shot this weekend.

00:01:13.306 --> 00:01:15.074
Congratulations.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:15.074 --> 00:01:16.943
-Thank you.

00:01:16.943 --> 00:01:18.578
-Is this what you
ended up wearing?

00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:21.147
-No. Jimmy, you know me
well enough to know

00:01:21.147 --> 00:01:22.181
I did not bring it.

00:01:22.181 --> 00:01:24.484
I was looking like
a hot-ass mess.

00:01:24.484 --> 00:01:28.321
I was in drawstring jeans
and mom sneakers.

00:01:28.321 --> 00:01:29.888
I didn't have a wig on.

00:01:29.888 --> 00:01:33.392
It was a hot mess.
Yeah. Yeah.

00:01:33.392 --> 00:01:35.795
-Buddy, you're doing
so many cool things.

00:01:35.795 --> 00:01:37.563
I want to make sure I hit
all the bases here.

00:01:37.563 --> 00:01:39.465
This first thing I want to
talk to you about is

00:01:39.465 --> 00:01:42.034
that you have another book
coming out this fall,

00:01:42.034 --> 00:01:44.537
and you posted the cover here.
Yeah, it says,

00:01:44.537 --> 00:01:47.040
"Please Don't Sit On My Bed
In Your Outside Clothes."

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:48.340
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:51.911
-Yes. Yes.
-This is your third book here.

00:01:51.911 --> 00:01:54.747
Has the process gotten
any easier?

00:01:54.747 --> 00:01:56.682
-It has.

00:01:56.682 --> 00:01:58.951
I feel like when I wrote
my first book, I was --

00:01:58.951 --> 00:02:01.487
Every day I was like
Claire Danes in "Homeland."

00:02:01.487 --> 00:02:03.723
I was just crying.
It was ugly.

00:02:03.723 --> 00:02:05.191
It was not cute.

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:06.959
But this time it was good.

00:02:06.959 --> 00:02:09.228
It was really good,
and the title is

00:02:09.228 --> 00:02:12.932
a public-service announcement
to white people

00:02:12.932 --> 00:02:17.837
to not sit on my bed
after you've been on a subway.

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:20.740
-Someone is passing out
in our audience right now.

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:22.208
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.208 --> 00:02:25.678
I've never heard this sound,
but when you said "wh-white,"

00:02:25.678 --> 00:02:27.747
someone almost --
-"Wh-White."

00:02:27.747 --> 00:02:30.650
-"Wh-White," yes.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:32.885
It's great to hear that laugh.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.885 --> 00:02:34.987
Gosh, I've missed the laughs.

00:02:34.987 --> 00:02:37.090
Speaking of the laughs,

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:39.291
you're about to hit
a stand-up milestone.

00:02:39.291 --> 00:02:41.861
You're getting your own special
on HBO.

00:02:41.861 --> 00:02:43.162
Phoebe Robinson.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:43.162 --> 00:02:44.596
-Yes!

00:02:44.596 --> 00:02:46.399
-That's a huge deal, bud!

00:02:46.399 --> 00:02:48.300
Phoebe.
-Thank you.

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:49.969
Thank you. I'm so excited.

00:02:49.969 --> 00:02:51.003
I'm so pumped up.

00:02:51.003 --> 00:02:53.139
I've been doing stand-up
for 13 years.

00:02:53.139 --> 00:02:55.775
And I'm glad that I'm finally
reaching this milestone.

00:02:55.775 --> 00:02:57.343
I'm pinching myself every day.

00:02:57.343 --> 00:02:58.911
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Good for you bud.

00:02:58.911 --> 00:03:01.947
Good for you. I love 'em!
So excited for you.

00:03:01.947 --> 00:03:04.016
I want to talk about
your new show.

00:03:04.016 --> 00:03:06.519
This is "Doing the Most
with Phoebe Robinson"

00:03:06.519 --> 00:03:07.753
on Comedy Central.

00:03:07.753 --> 00:03:10.757
You interview celebrities

00:03:10.757 --> 00:03:12.692
while also learning a new skill.

00:03:12.692 --> 00:03:14.694
-Yeah, so, basically I came up
with the show

00:03:14.694 --> 00:03:17.897
because I'm a type-A workaholic
and I have, like, no skills.

00:03:17.897 --> 00:03:20.432
I can't drive. I can't cook.
I can't start a fire.

00:03:20.432 --> 00:03:23.536
Like, if this was like the movie
"A Quiet Place,"

00:03:23.536 --> 00:03:26.039
I would just make a bunch of
noise so I could get killed

00:03:26.039 --> 00:03:28.240
so everyone else can survive.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:29.676
And so with this show,

00:03:29.676 --> 00:03:31.610
I just kind of wanted to learn
how to do different things,

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:34.480
like baking, some sort of
more physical stuff --

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:36.215
riding a horse with
Whitney Cummings.

00:03:36.215 --> 00:03:38.050
And it's been a lot of fun.

00:03:38.050 --> 00:03:40.786
I'm definitely learning
a lot of new skills.

00:03:40.786 --> 00:03:42.154
-We do that on our show, too.

00:03:42.154 --> 00:03:44.189
We play games with celebrities

00:03:44.189 --> 00:03:46.058
just so you see
a different side.

00:03:46.058 --> 00:03:47.893
And you do get in there.

00:03:47.893 --> 00:03:50.829
I actually like --
You do a thing called

00:03:50.829 --> 00:03:53.866
"Three Big Questions"
or three --

00:03:53.866 --> 00:03:56.035
-Yes.
-BQs.

00:03:56.035 --> 00:03:57.937
-Three BQs. Mm-hmm.

00:03:57.937 --> 00:04:01.541
-There's something interesting
about this interview style

00:04:01.541 --> 00:04:03.109
that we've not tried
on the show,

00:04:03.109 --> 00:04:06.679
but you --
you spoon with your guests.

00:04:06.679 --> 00:04:08.314
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.314 --> 00:04:10.583
-I mean, you know what?

00:04:10.583 --> 00:04:14.553
Yes, you have to, sometimes
as an excuse, to just sort of

00:04:14.553 --> 00:04:17.423
be close with a hot gentleman

00:04:17.423 --> 00:04:19.826
that I would have no chance with
in real life.

00:04:19.826 --> 00:04:21.093
[ Laughter ]

00:04:21.093 --> 00:04:23.396
But in all seriousness,
it's just really great.

00:04:23.396 --> 00:04:26.832
When you're, like, being held,
like, you let your guard down,

00:04:26.832 --> 00:04:27.967
and sometimes you'll be funny

00:04:27.967 --> 00:04:29.301
and sometimes
you'll be vulnerable.

00:04:29.301 --> 00:04:31.471
-What are you talking about?
-I think next time --

00:04:31.471 --> 00:04:33.039
-No, no, no.

00:04:33.039 --> 00:04:35.308
I can't spoon people
when they come on the show.

00:04:35.308 --> 00:04:36.275
[ Laughter ]
No.

00:04:36.275 --> 00:04:38.210
-Yes. Yes, you can.
-I cannot.

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:40.213
-You can spoon Michelle Obama.

00:04:40.213 --> 00:04:43.282
-No, I cannot spoon
Michelle Obama on the show!

00:04:43.282 --> 00:04:45.151
Absolutely not! You can.
-Yes, you can.

00:04:45.151 --> 00:04:46.551
-No. You can.

00:04:46.551 --> 00:04:47.887
I do want to show a clip.

00:04:47.887 --> 00:04:50.722
Here's Phoebe Robinson
and Kevin Bacon

00:04:50.722 --> 00:04:54.059
in this week's "Doing the Most
with Phoebe Robinson."

00:04:54.059 --> 00:04:55.361
Take a look at this.

00:04:55.361 --> 00:04:56.596
-Okay, so what do I do next?

00:04:56.596 --> 00:04:58.598
-So maybe just
a little sidestep,

00:04:58.598 --> 00:05:00.532
you know, kind of shimmy,
start moving.

00:05:00.532 --> 00:05:02.101
-But then what do I grab on to?

00:05:02.101 --> 00:05:03.302
I'm just holding the rope?

00:05:03.302 --> 00:05:04.403
-Yeah. Just hold on to the rope.

00:05:04.403 --> 00:05:07.072
And hold on tight --
-No, not the hoop.

00:05:07.072 --> 00:05:09.508
-One of my hoops just fell,
Kevin!

00:05:09.508 --> 00:05:11.177
-Oh, no.
'Cause we got to start again.

00:05:11.177 --> 00:05:13.679
-I just want to make a deal
that if I fall off this,

00:05:13.679 --> 00:05:16.148
I'm not getting back on,
and it's fine

00:05:16.148 --> 00:05:19.151
because, you know,
it's my civil rights.

00:05:19.151 --> 00:05:21.921
Martin Luther King Jr. fought
so I could say no

00:05:21.921 --> 00:05:23.990
to white nonsense
whenever I want.

00:05:23.990 --> 00:05:27.293
[ Laughter ]

00:05:27.293 --> 00:05:29.996
-Unbelievable.
You are unbelievable!

00:05:29.996 --> 00:05:31.997
I love you. Phoebe Robinson!

00:05:31.997 --> 00:05:35.301
"Doing the Most with
Phoebe Robinson" airs Fridays

00:05:35.301 --> 00:05:37.570
at 11:00 p.m. on Comedy Central.

